# Introduction to SIEM

Completed the Introduction to SIEM room on TryHackMe.

This room provided a foundational understanding of Security Information and Event Management (SIEM), including its role in monitoring, detecting, and investigating security events across an organization’s infrastructure.

## Topics Covered
- SIEM fundamentals
- Log collection and correlation
- Security event monitoring
- Alert generation and analysis
- SOC workflows and investigation basics

## Tools Used
- SIEM platform (conceptual / lab environment)
- Log analysis tools
- Security dashboards for event monitoring

## Summary
Through this lab, I learned how SIEM solutions aggregate and analyze log data from multiple sources such as endpoints, servers, and network devices. I also explored how detection rules are used to identify suspicious activity and generate alerts for SOC analysts.

This exercise reinforced how SIEM systems provide centralized visibility and support incident detection and response in a Security Operations Center (SOC) environment.

Overall, this room strengthened my understanding of how security teams use SIEM platforms to monitor threats and investigate security events effectively.
